          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "SEM micrographs giving a cross-sectional view of the molded part for the foamed COC as well as COC/CB3 and COC/cCF10 are shown in Figure 3."
        },
        {
          "block_id": "P_2_41",
          "page": 2,
          "bbox": [
            506.0,
            686.0,
            900.0,
            793.0
          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "Comparing SEM micrographs of the foamed and nonfoamed COC/ CB3, as seen in Figure 4, there was no detectable difference in CB dispersion caused by the foaming agent. The largest aggregates of CB found were 0.5 lm in both micrographs in comparison with the nominal cell diameter of 60 lm found in COC/CB3."
        },
        {
          "block_id": "I_3_48",
          "page": 3,
          "bbox": [
            106.0,
            630.0,
            480.0,
            876.0
          ],
          "source_type": "image",
          "source_sentence": "Figure 3 SEM image showing the cell morphology for (a) COC, (b) COC/CB3, and (c) COC/cCF10 composite in the LT plane. L, horizontal direction and T, vertical direction. Filler particles are not detectable at given resolution."
        },
        {
          "block_id": "I_3_52",
          "page": 3,
          "bbox": [
            512.0,
            651.0,
            893.0,
            887.0
          ],
          "source_type": "image",
          "source_sentence": "Figure 4 Close-up examination of fractured surface of COC/CB3 composite, (a) nonfoamed specimen and (b) foamed specimen, by SEM. CB appears as small clusters of spherical particles in the fractured surface of the matrix."
        }
      ],
      "confidence": {
